'=====================================================================
' Agent name : BulkReg\07 - Create Mail Files
' Version    : see VERSION (libraries BulkRegCommon + BulkRegAgents)
' Code       : ALL logic is in the script library BulkRegAgents (BR_RunCreateMailFiles).
'              This agent only calls it, so it never changes between releases.
'
' HOW TO INSTALL: open the agent, click in the editor, Ctrl+A, Delete, paste this
'              WHOLE file, Ctrl+S. Designer puts each part in its place automatically.
' Designer   : Shared agent, LotusScript
'              Runtime: On event > Action menu selection, Target: None
'              (NOT 'All selected documents' - Designer's default - or Notes asks for a selected document)
'              (backslash in the name = Actions > BulkReg submenu; do NOT use '|')
'
' What it does (details: BulkRegAgents > BR_RunCreateMailFiles):
'
' Second phase of the fast registration. With MailFileDeferred=1 in bulkreg.ini,
' 03 - Register Batch registers the users WITHOUT creating the mail files (the slow
' part). This agent then creates every mail file that the Person document names but
' that does not exist yet: from MailTemplate on the user's mail server, database title,
' ACL (MailACLManager + owner), and the AdminP cluster replica requests.
'
' Scope (asked at start): one batch file, or blank = all registered DirSync users.
' Existing mail files are never touched, so it can be re-run safely.
' DryRun=1 (default) only reports what it would create (WOULD_CREATE).
' Run it right after each 03 - Register Batch (mail cannot be delivered to a user until
' the mail file exists); it may run in a second Notes client during the next batch.
' Report: <BatchDir>\BATCH-<id>_mailcreate_<MODE>_<run>.csv + audit folder + log database.
'=====================================================================
'#####################################################################
' --- part 1: (Options) ---
'#####################################################################
Option Public
Option Declare
Use "BulkRegAgents"
'#####################################################################
' --- part 2: Initialize ---
'#####################################################################
Sub Initialize
	Call BR_RunCreateMailFiles()
End Sub
